<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Gg2.Tests</RootNamespace>

    <!--
      ⚠️ The ThreadPool floor, raised well above the core count, and it is not a
      performance tweak: without it WebAdminTests fails intermittently and the
      suite's exit code is red on a fast machine.

      WebAdminServer schedules its accept loop and every connection with
      Task.Run (WebAdminServer.cs:201, 276), so the panel under test answers on
      ThreadPool threads. xunit runs one collection per core, and the match
      tests among them hold a pool thread each for seconds at a time. The pool
      then injects new threads at roughly one or two a second, which is slower
      than the 20s HttpClient timeout WebAdminTests uses to mean "the panel is
      hung" - so a request that would be answered in a millisecond on an idle
      box is never scheduled at all, and a DIFFERENT web test times out on each
      run.

      Measured on a 24-core box, full suite, three runs per arm: default pool
      floor fails 3 of 3 (2m20s); MaxParallelThreads=4 passes but costs 2m52s;
      this floor passes at full parallelism in 2m00s. Diagnosing it from the
      failure is near impossible - the assertion never runs, the panel is fine
      in isolation (58/58), and the failing test moves.

      Nothing in the SERVER needs this. The starvation is the test harness's own
      parallelism, not something a deployment can do to itself: the tick loop is
      a dedicated thread and the sockets are async I/O. docs/WEBADMIN.md, "why
      the tests raise the ThreadPool floor".
    -->
    <ThreadPoolMinThreads>128</ThreadPoolMinThreads>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.12.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.8.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Protocol\Gg2.Protocol.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Maps\Gg2.Maps.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Server\Gg2.Server.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Simulation\Gg2.Simulation.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Bots\Gg2.Bots.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Nav\Gg2.Nav.csproj" />

    <!-- The command line itself. See CliCoverageTests. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Gg2.Host\Gg2.Host.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="Fixtures\**\*" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
